# 03 — Multi-Viewport Layout (ViewportGrid) — Revised for R3F + Synced Camera

## 1. Concept

Like 3ds Max — split viewport into multiple panes. All panes show the same model and share the same camera. Each pane controls which layers are visible and in which display mode.

**Key difference from 3ds Max:** Camera is always synchronized. You rotate in any pane → all panes rotate together. This makes the split useful for comparing different visualizations (vectors vs wireframe vs airbox) of the same scene from the same angle.

## 2. Layout Presets

```typescript
export type ViewportGridLayout =
  | "single"         // 1×1
  | "split-h"        // left + right
  | "split-v"        // top + bottom
  | "quad"           // 2×2
  | "one-plus-two";  // large left + two stacked right
```

```
single:        split-h:       quad:          one-plus-two:
┌──────────┐   ┌─────┬─────┐  ┌─────┬─────┐  ┌────────┬────┐
│  shaded  │   │vec  │wire │  │shade│wire │  │ shaded │wire│
│  +vec    │   │field│frame│  ├─────┼─────┤  │ +vec   ├────┤
└──────────┘   └─────┴─────┘  │air  │flat │  │        │air │
                               └─────┴─────┘  └────────┴────┘
```

## 3. Per-Pane Config

```typescript
interface ViewportPaneConfig {
  id: string;                    // "main" | "tl" | "tr" | "bl" | "br" | "left" | "right-1" | "right-2"
  label: string;                 // "Shaded" | "Wireframe" | "Vector Field" | "Airbox"
  displayMode: DisplayMode;
  layers: PaneLayerVisibility;
}

interface PaneLayerVisibility {
  meshSurface: boolean;
  scalarField: boolean;
  vectorGlyphs: boolean;
  wireframe: boolean;
  airbox: boolean;
  axesGrid: boolean;
  selection: boolean;
  clipPlane: boolean;
}
```

### Default Presets

| Layout | Panes |
|---|---|
| `single` | `[{ shaded, all layers on }]` |
| `split-h` | `[{ shaded, vectors on }, { wireframe, mesh only }]` |
| `quad` | `[{ shaded, all }, { wireframe, mesh }, { shaded, airbox only }, { flat-shaded, mesh }]` |
| `one-plus-two` | `[{ shaded, all }, { wireframe, mesh }, { shaded, airbox }]` |

## 4. Camera Synchronization

### Architecture

```
                    ┌─────────────────┐
                    │  Zustand Store   │
                    │  camera: {       │
                    │    position,     │
                    │    target,       │
                    │    up, fov       │
                    │  }               │
                    └────────┬────────┘
                             │
              ┌──────────────┼──────────────┐
              ▼              ▼              ▼
         ┌─────────┐   ┌─────────┐   ┌─────────┐
         │ Pane 1   │   │ Pane 2   │   │ Pane 3   │
         │ <Canvas> │   │ <Canvas> │   │ <Canvas> │
         │ Synced   │   │ Synced   │   │ Synced   │
         │ Controls │   │ Controls │   │ Controls │
         └─────────┘   └─────────┘   └─────────┘
```

Any pane's `SyncedOrbitControls` writes to the shared store. All panes read from it and `invalidate()` their canvas when camera changes.

### SyncedOrbitControls

```tsx
import { OrbitControls } from "@react-three/drei";
import { useThree } from "@react-three/fiber";

export function SyncedOrbitControls() {
  const controlsRef = useRef<OrbitControlsImpl>(null);
  const camera = useViewport3DStore((s) => s.camera);
  const setCamera = useViewport3DStore((s) => s.setCamera);
  const { invalidate } = useThree();

  // Write: user interaction → store
  const handleChange = useCallback(() => {
    const controls = controlsRef.current;
    if (!controls) return;
    setCamera({
      position: controls.object.position.toArray(),
      target: controls.target.toArray(),
    });
  }, [setCamera]);

  // Read: store → camera (from other pane's interaction)
  useEffect(() => {
    const controls = controlsRef.current;
    if (!controls) return;
    controls.object.position.fromArray(camera.position);
    controls.target.fromArray(camera.target);
    controls.update();
    invalidate();
  }, [camera, invalidate]);

  return <OrbitControls ref={controlsRef} onChange={handleChange} />;
}
```

### Performance

- Camera updates are in Zustand (fast, no re-render of React tree)
- Each `<Canvas>` subscribes to the camera state via `useViewport3DStore` selector
- `invalidate()` triggers a single R3F frame per pane
- 4 panes × 1 frame each = 4 frames per camera interaction — acceptable at 60fps

## 5. CSS Grid

```css
.fm-viewport-grid {
  display: grid;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  gap: 1px;
  background: var(--fm-surface-0);
}

.fm-viewport-grid[data-layout="single"]       { grid-template: 1fr / 1fr; }
.fm-viewport-grid[data-layout="split-h"]      { grid-template: 1fr / 1fr 1fr; }
.fm-viewport-grid[data-layout="split-v"]      { grid-template: 1fr 1fr / 1fr; }
.fm-viewport-grid[data-layout="quad"]         { grid-template: 1fr 1fr / 1fr 1fr; }
.fm-viewport-grid[data-layout="one-plus-two"] { grid-template: 1fr 1fr / 2fr 1fr; }
.fm-viewport-grid[data-layout="one-plus-two"] > :first-child { grid-row: 1 / -1; }
```

## 6. Pane Toolbar (per-pane)

Each pane gets a small overlay toolbar for:
- Display mode toggle (shaded / wireframe / shaded+wireframe)
- Layer toggles (vectors, airbox, wireframe, grid)
- Label showing current config

The toolbar is a DOM overlay positioned over the R3F canvas, not inside the Three.js scene.

## 7. Maximise / Restore

Double-click pane label → that pane fills the viewport. Other panes hidden via CSS (`display: none`) — their canvases don't render. Double-click again to restore.

## 8. Active Pane

Clicking inside a pane sets it as active (subtle border highlight). Active pane:
- Receives keyboard shortcuts (numpad camera presets)
- Is the target for toolbar commands
- Shows focus indicator

## 9. Keyboard Shortcuts

| Shortcut | Action |
|---|---|
| `Alt+1` | Single layout |
| `Alt+2` | Split horizontal |
| `Alt+3` | Split vertical |
| `Alt+4` | Quad |
| `Alt+5` | One + two |
| `Space` | Maximise/restore active pane |
| `Numpad 0` | Reset camera to perspective |
| `Numpad 1` | Front view |
| `Numpad 3` | Right view |
| `Numpad 7` | Top view |
| `Z` | Toggle wireframe on active pane |
| `V` | Toggle vectors on active pane |
| `A` | Toggle airbox on active pane |
